Verse 1:
[Ab]The [Db/Ab]church [Ab]has [Gdim]waited [Db/F]long
[Ab]Her [Db/Ab]absent [Gdim]Lord [Ab]to [Bbm]see;
[Cm]And still [Eb/Bb]in [Bbm]loneliness [Am]she [Bbm]waits,
[E/B]A [Fm/C]friendless [Ab]stranger [Cm/G]she.

Verse 2:
[Ab]How [Db/Ab]long, [Ab]O [Gdim]Lord [Ab]our [Db/F]God,
[Ab]Holy and [Gdim]true [Ab]and [Bbm]good,
[Cm]Wilt Thou [Eb/Bb]not [Bbm]judge Thy [Am]suffering [Bbm]church,
[E/B]Her [Fm/C]sighs [Ab]and tears [Bbm/F]and [Cm/G]blood?

Verse 3:
[Ab]We [Db/Ab]long [Ab]to [Gdim]hear [Ab]Thy [Db/F]voice,
[Ab]To [Db/Ab]see [Ab]Thee [Gdim]face [Ab]to [Bbm]face,
[Cm]To [Eb/Bb]share [Bbm]Thy crown [Am]and [Bbm]glory then,
[E/B]As [Fm/C]now [Ab]we share [Bbm/F]Thy [Cm/G]grace.

Verse 4:
[Ab]Come, [Db/Ab]Lord, [Ab]and [Gdim]wipe [Ab]away
[Ab]The [Db/Ab]curse, [Ab]the [Gdim]sin, [Ab]the [Bbm]stain,
[Cm]And [Eb/Bb]make [Bbm]this blighted world [Am]of [Bbm]ours
[E/B]Thine [Fm/C]own [Ab]fair world [Bbm/F]again.
